#: ../../source/docs/common-relay.rst:38
#: 60c17d2737164a3d82ce96cd548083cd
msgid ":ref:`RELAY2_PIN<RELAY2_PIN>`: the autopilot designated GPIO pin to be used for the function. See  the :ref:`common-gpios` page for information on how to determine the pin numbers and setup for using autopilot servo/motor outputs. DroneCAN peripherals with remote relay outputs have pin numbers in the 1000 to 1015 range. Consult the peripheral's documentation for proper pin number to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-relay.rst:39
#: f33d7dbcad1f4231ab92bcaf2f5a9fa6
msgid ":ref:`RELAY2_DEFAULT<RELAY2_DEFAULT>`: After boot up, should the relay default to ON (1) or OFF (0, default), or 2 = no change from bootloader state for the relay output pin. This only applies to RELAYx_FUNC \"Relay\" (1). All other uses will pick the appropriate default output state from within the controlling function's parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-relay.rst:40
#: 99eb9ef64e9b4fcbbf97967bf6c14b49
msgid ":ref:`RELAY2_INVERTED<RELAY2_INVERTED>`: this parameter controls the actual output voltage level corresponding to the \"ON\"  state. If set to \"1\", the ON will actually be a low output, versus the normal high output voltage level. Will also impact the :ref:`RELAY2_DEFAULT<RELAY2_DEFAULT>` output voltage level."
msgstr ""

